# Faultline Adversarial Engineering Gate

For substantial features, architecture changes, refactors, or security/concurrency-sensitive modifications:

1. Before writing code or proposals, run a Faultline preflight audit following `.agents/skills/faultline-preflight/SKILL.md` (or `skills/faultline-preflight/SKILL.md`).
2. Brownfield reconnaissance is mandatory: map packages, services, entry points, call graph, data stores, trust boundaries, and configuration.
3. Keep preflight strictly read-only: never modify production code, migrations, or configs during preflight analysis.
4. Stress-test execution paths: trace null/empty inputs, concurrency interleavings, retries, timeout/interruption scenarios.
5. Record findings with reproducible sequences and testable Given/When/Then scenarios before implementing changes.
